* Germanium Fuzz — exported from Lutherie
* The 1960s round fuzz: two leaky germanium PNP transistors, directly coupled, on a −9 V supply (positive ground). It cleans up when you turn the guitar down, because its input impedance is low enough to load the pickups.

Vsig SIGSRC 0 SIN(0 0.3 220.0) AC 1
Rsig SIGSRC IN 6k
CC1 IN N2 2.2u
QQ1 N3 N2 0 Q_GermaniumPNPAC128type
RR1 VCC_-9V N3 33k
QQ2 N5 N3 N6 Q_GermaniumPNPAC128type
RR2 N7 N5 470
RR3 VCC_-9V N7 8.2k
* Fuzz pot 1k B taper at 90%
RVR1a 0 N8 900
RVR1b N8 N6 100
CC2 0 N8 22u
RR4 N2 N6 100k
CC3 N7 N9 10n
* Volume pot 500k A taper at 60%
RVR2a 0 OUT 81k
RVR2b OUT N9 419k
Rload OUT 0 1Meg
VVS2 VCC_-9V 0 DC -9.0

.model Q_GermaniumPNPAC128type PNP(Is=1.2e-06 Bf=90.0 Br=5.0 Vaf=30.0 Nf=1.1 Cje=5e-11 Cjc=2e-11 Mje=0 Mjc=0)

.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-8 method=trap
.tran 1.3020833333333333e-06 0.3 0 1.3020833333333333e-06
.control
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=12
run
wrdata germanium_fuzz.ngspice.txt v(OUT)
.endc
.end